   5:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** extern SPI_HandleTypeDef hspi2;
   6:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** 
   7:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** /* SPI task: dequeues [gesture, intensity] packets posted by HAL_SPI_RxCpltCallback
   8:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    and maps them to shared audio effect parameters.
   9:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** 
  10:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    SPI2 is configured as a slave (SPI_MODE_0, MSB first, 8-bit, hardware NSS).
  11:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    The Raspberry Pi drives NSS and clocks two bytes per transaction:
  12:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****      Byte 0 — gesture  (1=volume, 2=chorus, 3=LPF, 4=pitch, 0/other=clear)
  13:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****      Byte 1 — intensity (0-255 mapped to the parameter range)
  14:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** 
  15:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    The ISR packs both bytes into a uint32_t (gesture << 8 | intensity) and posts
  16:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    to spiQueueHandle.  Reading from the queue is atomic, so there is no race with
  17:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    the DMA circular buffer.
  18:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** 
  19:Core/Src/spi_task.c ****    LED assignments (GPIOD): LD3=volume, LD5=reverb, LD3+LD5=LPF, LD4=pitch, all off=clear. */
  20:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** 
  21:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** void StartSPITask(void const *argument)
  22:Core/Src/spi_task.c **** {
